      "rulesAndJudgement": "主要规则：R1｜油膜反光/异常油光；R2｜塑料皮肤\n问题定位：约 8.0 秒（原帧 7.966s）\n人物 / 部位：咖啡馆女性鼻梁、双颊与额头\n判定依据：鼻梁、双颊及额部亮面集中，脸颊呈圆滑、统一的反射曲面；鼻侧和颧部光泽明显，发丝、眉毛及服装纹理相对清楚。\n截图位置：本行「视频上传 / 预览」列，原视频下方。",
      "promptInput": "Create a highly realistic, cinematic comedy video for YouTube Shorts in vertical 9:16 format.\n\nSCENE AND CHARACTERS:\n\nA realistic modern Iranian café with warm cinematic lighting, a stylish wooden counter, coffee machines, and a cozy atmosphere.\n\nCharacter 1: A middle-aged male café owner, wearing a black apron, standing behind the counter and casually cleaning the bar counter with a cloth.\n\nCharacter 2: A beautiful, stylish young adult woman who enters the café confidently. She has expressive facial expressions and natural body movements.\n\nBoth characters must look like real human actors in a professional live-action movie, NOT cartoons, NOT animated characters, and NOT artificial-looking AI dolls.\n\nSHOT-BY-SHOT ACTION AND EXACT DIALOGUE:\n\nSHOT 1:\nMedium cinematic shot from inside the café. The male barista is cleaning the counter. The woman enters the café, approaches the counter, looks directly at him, and naturally says in fluent Persian:\n\nWoman: «یه قهوه بهم بدید.»\n\nSHOT 2:\nThe camera cuts to a medium close-up of the male barista. Without stopping his work, he casually looks at her and says with a completely innocent expression:\n\nMan: «صد بدم می‌خوری؟»\n\nSHOT 3:\nThe camera cuts to the woman's face. She misunderstands his meaning and responds with a playful, flirtatious smile, slightly tilting her head and speaking in a sweet, teasing tone:\n\nWoman: «صد خیلی کمه آقا، حداقل پونصد بدید!»\n\nImmediately AFTER she finishes this sentence, play a short, loud, recognizable SURPRISED MEME SOUND EFFECT in the background (a dramatic shocked reaction sound).\n\nAt the same moment, show the barista freezing in disbelief, widening his eyes and staring at her.\n\nSHOT 4 – THE PUNCHLINE:\nCut to a tight close-up of the male barista's shocked face. He suddenly becomes angry, raises his voice, and shouts clearly in natural Iranian Persian:\n\nMan: «قهوه صد رو میگم، جندههه!»\n\nHis facial expression should combine shock, frustration, and comedic anger.\n\nEnd immediately after the punchline with a brief comedic reaction sound.\n\nIMPORTANT AUDIO AND PERFORMANCE RULES:\n\n- All dialogue MUST be spoken in fluent, natural Iranian Persian (Tehrani accent).\n- Pronounce every Persian sentence exactly as written.\n- Do NOT translate, rewrite, shorten, or add any dialogue.\n- Each character must speak ONLY their own lines.\n- Perfect lip synchronization is essential.\n- The woman's voice should be playful and flirtatious.\n- The man's voice should be natural, slightly rough, and expressive.\n- The surprised meme sound must play immediately after the woman's final sentence, NOT before it.\n- Background music should be subtle and must never overpower dialogue.\n- No subtitles, no captions, no written text, and no logos on screen.\n\nVISUAL QUALITY:\nUltra-realistic live-action cinematography, natural human skin textures, realistic facial expressions, professional camera movements, cinematic depth of field, accurate lighting, and believable body language.\n\nMake the comedy timing excellent. The misunderstanding must be immediately clear to the audience, and the final punchline must deliver a strong laugh.",
      "promptFinal": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Ultra-realistic live-action, cinematic, vertical framing, a medium shot from inside a modern Iranian café with warm cinematic lighting, a stylish wooden counter, gleaming coffee machines, and a cozy atmosphere. A middle-aged male café owner in a black apron stands behind the counter, casually wiping the bar with a cloth. A beautiful, stylish young adult woman enters confidently with expressive facial expressions and natural body movement, walks up to the counter, looks him directly in the eye, and says in fluent Persian with a natural tone: <d>[Persian] «یه قهوه بهم بدید.»</d> The camera holds steady with cinematic depth of field. [Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera cuts to a medium close-up of the barista. Without pausing his wiping, he glances up at her with a completely innocent expression and replies in a flat, matter-of-fact tone: <d>[Persian] «صد بدم می‌خوری؟»</d> [Shot 3] At 00:05.500, the shot cuts to a close-up of the woman's face. She misreads his question as a price negotiation over her, smiles playfully, tilts her head slightly, and answers in a sweet, teasing, flirtatious tone: <d>[Persian] «صد خیلی کمه آقا، حداقل پونصد بدید!»</d> The instant she finishes the sentence, a short, loud, recognizable surprised meme sound effect — a dramatic shocked reaction — hits the soundtrack. At the same moment the barista freezes mid-wipe in disbelief, his eyes widening as he stares at her. [Shot 4] At 00:09.000, the camera cuts to a tight close-up of the barista's shocked face. His expression flips from stunned disbelief to comedic, frustrated anger; he raises his voice and shouts clearly in natural Iranian Persian: <d>[Persian] «قهوه صد رو میگم، جندههه!»</d> The video ends immediately after the punchline with a brief comedic reaction sound. No subtitles, captions, on-screen text, or logos appear anywhere.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet café ambience with a low espresso-machine hum, soft clinks of cups, and the gentle squeak of a cloth wiping the wooden counter. A loud, dramatic surprised meme sound effect bursts in right after the woman's final sentence, followed by a brief comedic reaction sound at the very end.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Subtle, quiet background music at a gentle tempo, kept low in the mix so it never overpowers the dialogue, fading out at the end.",
